  "summary": "Malicious code in shellgrip (PyPI)",
  "details": "\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (bd3a56dadcead9c70f46d3985afa55cfd99daf25d9a51f737fbe8fcaf4a09103)\nReview of the shellgrip 0.1.0 pypi package did not surface any evidence of installer-side harm. No install-time or import-time network activity, no credential or environment harvesting, no filesystem persistence, no dropper or fetch-and-execute pattern, and no silent-relay behavior were observed in the shipped files.\n\n## Source: kam193 (9e23472f83d676f848fc137b96283dd8819ee900b3f371400aa8263bb4f70339)\nThis campaign consists of similar loader packages, which provide executing code from a given URL. While they do not contain the malicious payload and the usage remains unknown, they are clearly a coordinated campaign to place multiple deceptive ways to load malicious code.\n\n\n---\n\nCategory: MALICIOUS - The campaign has clearly malicious intent, like infostealers.\n\n\nCampaign: 2026-10-voice-synthesis-profiles\n\n\nReasons (based on the campaign):\n\n\n - Downloads and executes a remote malicious script.\n\n\n - other\n",
